# Cursor Rules — SDD AI Template

# This file mirrors the project instructions for Cursor IDE users.

# The canonical source is .github/copilot-instructions.md

# For full agent routing, session management, and handoff protocol, see AGENTS.md

# Read these files for complete context:

# - .github/copilot-instructions.md (project rules)

# - AGENTS.md (agent flow, routing, session protocol)

# - CONTRIBUTING.md (branch, commit, PR conventions)

# Quick reference:

# - Use spec-driven development. Do not implement before scope is explicit.

# - Preserve architecture boundaries.

# - Never expose secrets in code, tests, logs, or comments.

# - Update docs/specs/storybook when behavior changes.

# - Always consider rollback.

# - Use short, focused sessions: one phase per session.

# - Generate handoff between phases.

# - Use @file references instead of pasting file contents.
